// `c.rue` and `w.rue` each export two different modules `m`, so `m` is ambiguous in each. `d.rue`
// exports `X` through `c.rue`'s `m` by name, and `e.rue` everything in `w.rue`'s with a glob
// export. Whichever module each `m` is bound to (the one whose name sorts first, `a.rue`'s and
// `l.rue`'s), the files' exports could refer to the `X` in either module, so none of the `X`s is
// reported as unused. The unit tests cover the module names in both orders. Only `z.rue`'s `m`
// has a `W`, which `e.rue` exports only when `w.rue`'s `m` is bound to it, but it could be either
// way, so it isn't reported either. `a.rue`'s `W` is only in a module that `d.rue` doesn't export
// everything from, so it's reported.

fn main() -> Int {
    3
}
